  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Fray Mat&#xed;as de C&#xf3;rdova Human Rights Centre was awarded &#x20ac;10,000 for the implementation of project Contribute to capacity building for access to human rights for migrants and refugees on Mexico&apos;s southern border.The project aims to provide advice to asylum seekers as well as legal and psychosocial accompaniment focused on specific circumstances with a focus on gender, intersectional and children and adolescents, while at the same time allowing for a response to specific situations of serious human rights violations through specialised defence and strategic litigation.</narrative>
  </description>
